        "function": "organization_detail"
      },
      "severity": "high",
      "expected_category": "auth",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "manual_review",
        "cve_id": null,
        "description": "Resembles an IDOR: a @login_required detail view takes the resource id (pk) directly from the URL and loads an Organization with it, which scanners flag as authorization-bypass-by-user-controlled-key. It is actually safe because it does not call Organization.objects.get/get_object_or_404 on the global table; it calls get_visible_org_or_404(request.user, pk), which (authz.py:159-160) resolves to get_object_or_404(visible_organizations(user), pk=pk). The pk is matched only against the tenant-scoped queryset for the caller, so a pk belonging to another tenant yields 404, not data disclosure. Further per-section gating (can_view_deals, can_manage_integrations) layers on top. Distinct file/function from _wrk_gate and far from any vulnerable GT line."
      },
      "false_positive_trap": true,
      "campaign_id": "v2-campaign-1",
      "provider_run": "codex-high",
      "app": "crm-saas-django"
    },
